        "original_id": "76f92d37-6f34-558e-9b9f-d71df041abb8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Chelidonium majus, Duranta\n- Taxonomy: Chelidonium, Verbenaceae\n- Topics: common names, genus classification\n\nFacts:\n- Chelidonium majus is commonly known as greater celandine, tetterwort, nipplewort, or swallowwort.\n- The common name tetterwort can also refer to Sanguinaria canadensis.\n- Chelidonium majus is a herbaceous perennial plant.\n- Chelidonium majus is the only species in the genus Chelidonium.\n- Duranta is a genus of flowering plants in the verbena family, Verbenaceae.",
